      "body": {
        "text": "Strawberries can help your baby absorb MORE iron 👀\n\nStrawberries aren’t particularly high in iron themselves, but they’re rich in vitamin C, which helps your baby’s body absorb non-heme iron (the type found in plant-based foods).\n\nAnd that’s especially important when starting solids. \n\nAround 6 months, babies’ iron stores begin to decline, making iron-rich foods an important part of their diet.\n\nTry pairing strawberries with:\n\n🥣 Iron-fortified baby oatmeal\n🫘 Lentils or beans\n🌱 Tofu\n🥜 Smooth, thinned nut butter (once you’ve ruled out allergies)\n\nWant to know how to safely serve each of these foods?\n\n➡️ Try a super simple search in the Solid Starts app. Tap the link in our bio to learn more.\n\n#StartingSolids #BabyLedWeaning #BabyNutrition #IronRichFoods #FirstFoods"
      },
